### 3.12. Field Mixins / Explorer / Utilities (`fields/`)

* **`mixins/ArrayField.js`**: A mixin applied to field prototypes.
    ```typescript
    // Likely a function that modifies a Field prototype or class
    type KeystoneArrayFieldMixinFunction = (fieldClass: any, options?: any) => void;
    // Or an interface if it's an object with methods to be mixed in
    interface KeystoneArrayFieldMixin { /* ... methods ... */ }
    ```
* **`explorer/server.js`**: Sets up the field explorer UI/API.
    ```typescript
    // A function that likely adds routes to the Keystone Express app
    type KeystoneFieldExplorerServerFunction = (keystone: Keystone) => void;
    ```
* **`utils/*.js`**: Specific utility functions.
    ```typescript
    type KeystoneAddPresenceToQueryFunction = (query: any, fieldPath: string) => void;
    type KeystoneDefinePrototypeGettersFunction = (proto: any, getters: Record<string, () => any>) => void;
    type KeystoneBindFunctionsFunction = (obj: any, methodNames: string[]) => void;
    type KeystoneEvalDependsOnFunction = (dependsOn: Record<string, any> | undefined, values: Record<string, any>) => boolean;
    ```

## 4. Conclusion

By following these patterns, we can ensure the remaining type definitions are consistent with the existing ones and accurately reflect the structure of KeystoneJS v4. Remember to consult the actual source code (`Sources:` links) when defining the specifics of options interfaces and function signatures. Good luck!